后续提醒。

1054
00:42:14.140 --> 00:42:14.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1055
00:42:15.140 --> 00:42:19.120
Which is why Kevin does not come forward when he gets himself, because he would have had
这就是为什么凯文在惹上麻烦时不敢站出来，因为他不得不告诉我。

1056
00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:19.760
to tell me.
他确实得告诉我。

1057
00:42:19.900 --> 00:42:20.460
He would have.
他会的。

1058
00:42:20.600 --> 00:42:20.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1059
00:42:20.920 --> 00:42:21.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1060
00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:22.100
You know what?
你知道吗？

1061
00:42:23.500 --> 00:42:26.720
I really relate to Angela on so many levels.
我在很多层面上都对安吉拉感同身受。

1062
00:42:26.860 --> 00:42:27.280
Listen.
听着。

1063
00:42:27.500 --> 00:42:28.060
Really do.
真的。

1064
00:42:28.300 --> 00:42:31.100
There's on some levels, you're way more Angela than I am.
在某些层面上，你比我更像安吉拉。

1065
00:42:31.240 --> 00:42:31.640
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

1066
00:42:31.640 --> 00:42:36.640
I mean, I would have generated two, three, four very detailed emails about the party,
我是说，我会为派对和计划写两封、三封甚至四封非常详细的邮件。

1067
00:42:36.880 --> 00:42:37.760
the plans.
关于计划的。

1068
00:42:38.060 --> 00:42:38.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1069
00:42:38.880 --> 00:42:45.660
If I assigned someone to do lights for the tree and that's what I got, I would feel so
如果我指派某人去布置树上的灯，结果却搞成这样，我会感到非常

1070
00:42:45.660 --> 00:42:46.920
pissed and let down.
生气和失望。

1071
00:42:47.120 --> 00:42:51.140
If people went over the $20 budget, you would have been furious.
如果有人超出了20美元的预算，你肯定会大发雷霆的。

1072
00:42:51.340 --> 00:42:51.680
Furious.
暴跳如雷。

1073
00:42:51.760 --> 00:42:53.100
Because you would have been like, what's the point?
因为你会觉得，那有什么意义呢？

1074
00:42:53.380 --> 00:42:55.040
Why even have that number?
为什么要设那个限额呢？

1075
00:42:55.200 --> 00:42:56.160
Is Angela wrong?
安吉拉错了吗？

1076
00:42:56.460 --> 00:42:58.320
No, I don't think she's wrong.
不，我不觉得她错了。

1077
00:42:58.320 --> 00:43:03.020
She's just, you know, why is no one helping her?
她只是，你知道的，为什么没人帮她呢？

1078
00:43:03.220 --> 00:43:04.960
She's a by-the-book person.
她是个循规蹈矩的人。

1079
00:43:05.000 --> 00:43:05.280
She is.
确实是。

1080
00:43:05.280 --> 00:43:06.800
Why can't people follow the rules?
为什么人们就不能遵守规则呢？

1081
00:43:06.920 --> 00:43:07.420
I agree.
我同意。

1082
00:43:07.860 --> 00:43:13.820
So at nine minutes, 39 seconds, she gets pissed off on a whole new level because, as you were
所以在9分39秒时，她达到了全新的愤怒高度，因为正如你所说，

1083
00:43:13.820 --> 00:43:20.300
saying, this is when Michael is really ticked off that he got the oven mitt and he switches
这时迈克尔因为收到烤箱手套而非常恼火，于是他改变了派对规则。

1084
00:43:20.300 --> 00:43:20.880
the party.
不再玩秘密圣诞老人了。

1085
00:43:21.080 --> 00:43:22.240
No more Secret Santa.
他说，现在我们要玩“扬基交换”。

1086
00:43:22.240 --> 00:43:23.960
He says, now we're doing Yankee Swap.
是的。

1087
00:43:24.220 --> 00:43:24.540
Yes.
“扬基交换”或者“白象交换”，或者他还说了别的什么？

1088
00:43:24.960 --> 00:43:28.580
Yankee Swap slash White Elephant slash, what was the other one he said?
“肮脏圣诞节”。

1089
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:29.640
Nasty Christmas.
“肮脏圣诞节”。

1090
00:43:29.900 --> 00:43:30.480
Nasty Christmas.
你知道，其实当时关于这叫什么名字还有过一点小争论。

1091
00:43:30.820 --> 00:43:34.040
You know, there was actually a little debate about, what do you call it?
有人说，嗯，我们叫它“白象交换”。

1092
00:43:34.100 --> 00:43:36.080
And people were like, well, we call it White Elephant.
另一个人说，我们叫它“扬基交换”。

1093
00:43:36.140 --> 00:43:37.560
And someone else was like, we call it Yankee Swap.
我觉得编剧们把这些都写进了剧集里。

1094
00:43:37.640 --> 00:43:40.140
And I feel like the writers took that and put it in the episode.
是啊。

1095
00:43:40.460 --> 00:43:40.780
Yeah.
我把它叫做“扬基交换”。

1096
00:43:40.880 --> 00:43:42.520
I know it as Yankee Swap.
你把它叫做什么？

1097
00:43:42.760 --> 00:43:43.500
What do you know it as?
我以前叫它“白象交换”。

1098
00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:44.440
I knew it as White Elephant.
是啊。

1099
00:43:44.540 --> 00:43:44.740
Yeah.
我觉得他们这样做挺好的。

1100
00:43:45.080 --> 00:43:46.320
I think it's good they did that.
我觉得他们这样做挺好的。

1101
00:43:46.520 --> 00:43:47.020
I do too.
我也是。

1102
00:43:52.240 --> 00:43:52.520
Yes.
是的。

1103
00:43:52.660 --> 00:43:54.200
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢它了。

1104
00:43:54.380 --> 00:43:57.940
You know, here's something that I heard in the commentary, Angela, since we're talking
你知道吗，安吉拉，既然我们在谈论你的角色，

1105
00:43:57.940 --> 00:43:58.760
about your character.
我听过一段评论音轨，

1106
00:43:58.760 --> 00:44:02.000
I guess that you had a talking head in the fire.
我猜你在火灾那集有个访谈镜头。

1107
00:44:02.280 --> 00:44:04.820
I watched it because I have a DVD player now.
我看了，因为我现在有DVD播放机了。

1108
00:44:05.040 --> 00:44:05.720
Where you cried.
就是你哭的那段。

1109
00:44:05.900 --> 00:44:06.240
Yes.
是的。

1110
00:44:06.320 --> 00:44:07.320
In the deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1111
00:44:07.560 --> 00:44:12.460
Well, Mike said that the writer's room was so impressed with your performance and that
迈克说编剧室对你的表演和那个访谈镜头印象非常深刻，

1112
00:44:12.460 --> 00:44:18.180
talking head that they put a card on the wall that was Angela cries and they wanted
以至于他们在墙上贴了一张卡片写着“安吉拉哭泣”，他们想

1113
00:44:18.180 --> 00:44:21.660
to find an episode where you could cry a bunch and this was it.
找一集能让你大哭一场的戏，就是这一集了。

1114
00:44:21.660 --> 00:44:25.960
Mike sure told me, he said, I love to see your character cry.
迈克确实跟我说过，他说，我喜欢看你的角色哭。

1115
00:44:26.800 --> 00:44:32.660
He said, she's so pulled together that when you sort of fall apart, it's like really sort
他说，她平时总是那么严谨，所以当你崩溃的时候，

1116
00:44:32.660 --> 00:44:33.660
of oddly pleasing.
感觉真的很奇妙，让人很满足。

1117
00:44:34.280 --> 00:44:36.720
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

1118
00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:37.460
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

1119
00:44:37.540 --> 00:44:42.820
So yes, at nine minutes, 51 seconds, I have a talking head and my character is really upset
所以没错，在9分51秒的时候，我有一个访谈镜头，我的角色非常难过，

1120
00:44:42.820 --> 00:44:46.180
because she feels like Michael should have talked to the PPC firSt.
因为她觉得迈克尔应该先和派对策划委员会商量。

1121
00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:46.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1122
00:44:46.760 --> 00:44:47.520
Well, they should have.
嗯，他们确实应该商量的。

1123
00:44:47.760 --> 00:44:48.960
I mean, he should have.
我是说，他应该商量的。

1124
00:44:49.120 --> 00:44:50.440
And then she breaks down.
然后她就崩溃了。

1125
00:44:50.640 --> 00:44:53.140
So she is really starting to spiral.
所以她真的开始失控了。

1126
00:44:53.140 --> 00:44:55.760
And then when we cut back to the scene, she's still sobbing.
然后当我们切回那个场景时，她还在抽泣。

1127
00:44:55.880 --> 00:44:57.640
I mean, she's not sobbing, but she's still crying.
我是说，不算抽泣，但她还在哭。

1128
00:44:57.780 --> 00:44:58.360
She's sullen.
她闷闷不乐的。

1129
00:44:58.540 --> 00:44:59.480
She's very sullen.
她非常闷闷不乐。

1130
00:44:59.680 --> 00:44:59.880
Okay.
好吧。

1131
00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:03.040
You know, this famous line, Yankee swap.
你知道，那句名台词，“洋基交换”。

1132
00:45:03.280 --> 00:45:03.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1133
00:45:03.860 --> 00:45:04.400
From Michael.
迈克尔说的。

1134
00:45:04.840 --> 00:45:05.540
All right.
好的。

1135
00:45:05.780 --> 00:45:06.580
Mike sure.
迈克尔。

1136
00:45:07.100 --> 00:45:11.060
That's a written line that wasn't improvised that Steve would say Yankee swap.
那句台词是写在剧本里的，不是史蒂夫即兴发挥说“洋基交换”的。

1137
00:45:11.060 --> 00:45:16.200
And Mike wrote in the script in parentheses, crazy voice.
迈克在剧本的括号里写着：疯狂的声音。

1138
00:45:17.180 --> 00:45:20.420
And he, he was like, I know Steve will do something great with that.
他当时觉得，我知道史蒂夫会用那种方式演绎得很棒。

1139
00:45:20.640 --> 00:45:22.660
And that was Steve's take on that.
那就是史蒂夫对那句台词的处理。

1140
00:45:22.660 --> 00:45:23.560
Because they would do that.
因为他们经常那样做。

1141
00:45:23.660 --> 00:45:26.960
They would sometimes put little pieces of direction in the script for us.
他们有时会在剧本里给我们写一些简短的指导。

1142
00:45:27.100 --> 00:45:28.380
And then we'd have to interpret it.
然后我们就得去诠释它。

1143
00:45:28.600 --> 00:45:28.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1144
00:45:29.180 --> 00:45:32.740
Guys, did you notice in this episode, it is snowing outside.
伙计们，你们注意到这一集外面在下雪了吗？

1145
00:45:32.740 --> 00:45:34.460
I loved this touch.
我很喜欢这个细节。

1146
00:45:34.700 --> 00:45:38.160
I love that they kept cutting to the windows and there'd be snow.
我喜欢他们不断切换到窗户的镜头，外面总是飘着雪。

1147
00:45:38.580 --> 00:45:40.640
Do you remember how much fun it was to have the snow?
你们还记得有雪是多有趣吗？

1148
00:45:40.800 --> 00:45:41.860
We were so tickled.
我们当时高兴坏了。

1149
00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:42.520
We were.
我们确实是。

1150
00:45:42.520 --> 00:45:43.060
By the snow.
因为那些雪。

1151
00:45:43.240 --> 00:45:43.780
So excited.
太兴奋了。

1152
00:45:43.960 --> 00:45:47.840
You guys remember, we mostly just filmed inside and we never even saw outside or what
你们还记得吗，我们大部分时间都在室内拍摄，甚至从来没见过外面或者外面发生了什么。

1153
00:45:47.840 --> 00:45:48.700
was happening outside.
发生了什么。

1154
00:45:49.100 --> 00:45:49.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1155
00:45:49.220 --> 00:45:52.760
And so the fact that we had this extra element happening was so fun.
所以能有这种额外的元素加入真的太有趣了。

1156
00:45:52.920 --> 00:45:56.560
We really did film inside in a windowless warehouse.
我们确实是在一个没有窗户的仓库里拍摄的。

1157
00:45:56.940 --> 00:45:58.600
All the windows were fake.
所有的窗户都是假的。

1158
00:45:58.760 --> 00:46:00.480
They just had backdrops behind them.
后面只是挂了背景板。

1159
00:46:00.700 --> 00:46:00.820
Yeah.
没错。

1160
00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:04.620
So to see actual sunshine or snow or air was really exciting to us.
所以能看到真正的阳光、雪或者空气，对我们来说真的很令人兴奋。

1161
00:46:04.740 --> 00:46:06.660
I have a ton of facts about the snow.
关于雪，我有一大堆冷知识。

1162
00:46:06.820 --> 00:46:10.360
I don't know if anyone else will find it interesting, but I had written all about it
我不知道别人会不会觉得有趣，但我已经在我的博客兼日记里写过关于它的一切了。

1163
00:46:10.900 --> 00:46:13.120
in one of my blogs slash journals.
写过关于它的一切了。

1164
00:46:13.420 --> 00:46:14.600
I'm living for this.
我太期待了。

1165
00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:16.000
I can't wait to hear about it.
我迫不及待想听听了。

1166
00:46:16.140 --> 00:46:16.400
All right.
好吧。

1167
00:46:16.560 --> 00:46:17.120
I do have to pee.
我得去上个厕所。

1168
00:46:17.980 --> 00:46:21.680
Oh, do you want me to give you some snow facts when we come back from the break?
噢，你想让我等我们休息回来再讲雪的冷知识吗？

1169
00:46:21.940 --> 00:46:22.820
I mean, can I help you?
我是说，我能帮你什么吗？

1170
00:46:22.820 --> 00:46:26.040
You should be on an empty bladder when I lay these awesome facts on you.
我讲这些超棒的冷知识时，你最好排空膀胱。

1171
00:46:26.240 --> 00:46:28.980
You don't tell me or my bladder what we're doing.
你管不着我，也管不着我的膀胱。

1172
00:46:29.120 --> 00:46:29.840
Well, what do you want?
好吧，那你想要什么？

1173
00:46:29.940 --> 00:46:33.240
Do you want full bladder snow facts or empty bladder snow facts?
你是想要膀胱充盈时的雪知识，还是排空后的雪知识？

1174
00:46:33.240 --> 00:46:34.840
I want empty bladder snow facts.
我想要排空后的雪知识。

1175
00:46:34.840 --> 00:46:35.180
All right.
好吧。

1176
00:46:35.260 --> 00:46:36.120
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

1177
00:46:36.120 --> 00:46:40.120
Oh, I thought you were telling me that I had to not drink any more water or tea.
噢，我还以为你在告诉我，我不能再喝水或茶了。

1178
00:46:40.660 --> 00:46:44.120
When we go on a road trip, my husband will be like, can you not get an iced tea?
我们去公路旅行时，我丈夫总会说，你能不能别买冰茶了？

1179
00:46:44.940 --> 00:46:51.260
Okay, clearly you're projecting some other thing on me because I said I thought you should
好吧，显然你把别的事情投射到我身上了，因为我刚才说的是我觉得你应该为了听雪的知识去排空膀胱，她要走了。

1180
00:46:51.260 --> 00:46:53.620
empty your bladder for the snow facts she's leaving.
排空膀胱，她要走了。

1181
00:46:53.880 --> 00:46:56.460
First, you push away from the mic to eat your snack.
首先，你得先从麦克风前挪开去吃你的零食。

1182
00:46:56.880 --> 00:46:57.900
This is for you, Jenna.
这是给你的，珍娜。

1183
00:47:00.450 --> 00:47:01.330
It's so disgusting.
太恶心了。

1184
00:47:01.430 --> 00:47:02.750
Those are high nut Cheerios.
那是高坚果含量的麦圈。

1185
00:47:03.490 --> 00:47:04.330
Oh, God.
天哪。

1186
00:47:04.330 --> 00:47:19.400
For letting me have my bathroom break, I want to hear all about your snow.
为了让你让我去上厕所，我想听听关于你那些雪的事儿。

1187
00:47:19.720 --> 00:47:20.100
All right.
好吧。

1188
00:47:20.100 --> 00:47:25.720
I hope this isn't anticlimactic for people, but the company that came to make the snow
希望这对大家来说不会虎头蛇尾，但那家来造雪的公司叫“雪生意”。

1189
00:47:25.720 --> 00:47:27.040
is called Snow Business.
叫“雪生意”。

1190
00:47:27.460 --> 00:47:29.000
I love that.
我喜欢这个名字。

1191
00:47:29.300 --> 00:47:29.980
Snow Business.
“雪生意”。

1192
00:47:30.180 --> 00:47:31.000
Snow Business.
“雪生意”。

1193
00:47:31.000 --> 00:47:31.800
I remembered.
我记住了。

1194
00:47:32.100 --> 00:47:33.260
I remembered that.
我记住了那个名字。

1195
00:47:33.500 --> 00:47:34.520
It so tickled me.
它真的戳中我的笑点了。

1196
00:47:34.900 --> 00:47:37.400
Okay, so here's how it works with fake snow.
好了，人造雪是这样运作的。

1197
00:47:37.740 --> 00:47:39.660
There's a guy from Snow Business.
有个来自“雪生意”公司的人。

1198
00:47:39.660 --> 00:47:40.820
He shows up.
他会过来。

1199
00:47:40.960 --> 00:47:46.900
Now, the snow that falls from the sky is different from the ground cover snow.
现在，从天而降的雪和地上的积雪是不一样的。

1200
00:47:47.220 --> 00:47:49.140
The snow on the ground is snow.
地上的雪就是雪。

1201
00:47:49.400 --> 00:47:54.800
The snow that falls from the sky, I know, because it falls on my character at the end,
我知道从天而降的雪，因为最后它落在了我的角色身上，

1202
00:47:54.820 --> 00:47:56.520
and it is not snow.
但那并不是雪。

1203
00:47:56.640 --> 00:47:57.540
It's not snow.
那不是雪。

1204
00:47:57.600 --> 00:47:58.420
It's soap.
那是肥皂。

1205
00:47:58.680 --> 00:47:59.200
Yes.
是的。

1206
00:47:59.220 --> 00:48:00.620
You can get a choice.
你可以有选择。

1207
00:48:00.820 --> 00:48:04.840
You can get a choice of cornstarch, plastic, or soap.
你可以选择玉米淀粉、塑料或肥皂。

1208
00:48:04.840 --> 00:48:09.060
And Greg watched a demonstration of all three, and he picked soap.
格雷格看了这三种的演示，他选了肥皂。

1209
00:48:09.400 --> 00:48:15.540
Well, when by accident, a little piece of that might get in your mouth, it tastes like
嗯，如果不小心有一小块进了嘴里，尝起来就像

1210
00:48:15.540 --> 00:48:15.940
soap.
肥皂。

1211
00:48:16.140 --> 00:48:18.940
Because I shriek, and a piece of it went in my mouth.
因为我尖叫了一声，结果有一块进了我嘴里。

1212
00:48:20.060 --> 00:48:21.820
That's what she said.
她就是这么说的。

1213
00:48:22.280 --> 00:48:22.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1214
00:48:22.820 --> 00:48:23.220
Okay.
好吧。

1215
00:48:23.540 --> 00:48:25.600
On the ground, though, it's real snow.
不过地上的雪是真的。

1216
00:48:25.920 --> 00:48:30.200
And they bring this machine, and I don't know exactly how it works, but it's kind of
他们带来了一台机器，我不太清楚它具体是怎么运作的，但它有点

1217
00:48:30.200 --> 00:48:33.500
like a wood chipper, but in reverse.
像碎木机，不过是反向的。

1218
00:48:33.500 --> 00:48:36.480
It looks like something out of a Dr. Seuss book.
看起来就像苏斯博士书里的东西。

1219
00:48:36.820 --> 00:48:37.080
It does.
确实。

1220
00:48:37.380 --> 00:48:38.260
It really does.
真的像。

1221
00:48:38.520 --> 00:48:40.840
And it really blows snow.
而且它真的能喷出雪来。

1222
00:48:41.140 --> 00:48:42.440
I guess that's what it looks like.
我想看起来就是那样。

1223
00:48:42.500 --> 00:48:44.980
It looks like a snowblower, but it generates snow.
它看起来像吹雪机，但它能制造雪。

1224
00:48:45.220 --> 00:48:49.600
And then it just blows it all over the ground, all over the cars, and all that stuff.
然后它就把雪喷得到处都是，车上到处都是，诸如此类。

1225
00:48:49.800 --> 00:48:56.400
But guys, remember, this is like, we're shooting this in like October in Los Angeles, and it's
但伙计们，记住，我们是在十月份的洛杉矶拍摄的，而且

1226
00:48:56.400 --> 00:48:57.400
hot in October.
十月份很热。

1227
00:48:57.460 --> 00:48:59.180
It stays warm here.
这里一直很暖和。

1228
00:48:59.420 --> 00:48:59.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1229
00:48:59.600 --> 00:49:02.660
In the daytime, it's still in the mid-80s, 90s.
白天温度还在华氏80多度到90多度之间。

1230
00:49:03.160 --> 00:49:07.060
But it was night, and so we had a little bit of time with it.
但那是晚上，所以我们有一点时间用它。

1231
00:49:07.140 --> 00:49:09.000
I mean, it was still warm out.
我是说，外面还是很暖和。

1232
00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:09.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1233
00:49:09.460 --> 00:49:11.740
It was probably like in the high 60s.
大概有华氏60多度吧。

1234
00:49:11.860 --> 00:49:12.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1235
00:49:12.420 --> 00:49:13.560
That sounds about right.
听起来差不多。

1236
00:49:13.840 --> 00:49:14.100
All right.
好吧。

1237
00:49:14.100 --> 00:49:18.280
But yes, we were very excited to have snow, and Jenna, we're-
但是没错，我们非常兴奋能有雪，而且珍娜，我们……

1238
00:49:18.280 --> 00:49:19.660
Did you like my snow facts?
你喜欢我的雪知识吗？

1239
00:49:19.940 --> 00:49:20.400
I love-
我喜欢……

1240
00:49:20.400 --> 00:49:23.640
I feel a little vulnerable about them now, because we set them up so much.
我现在对这些知识感到有点不安，因为我们之前铺垫得太多了。

1241
00:49:23.740 --> 00:49:25.520
I mean, there was like a break, and-
我是说，中间休息了一下，然后……

1242
00:49:25.520 --> 00:49:25.900
No.
不。

1243
00:49:25.900 --> 00:49:27.060
I'm in my head about it.
我有点钻牛角尖了。

1244
00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:28.460
I like your snow facts.
我喜欢你的雪知识。

1245
00:49:28.780 --> 00:49:29.320
Snow business.
雪生意（Snow business）。

1246
00:49:29.700 --> 00:49:30.520
That's cute.
真可爱。

1247
00:49:30.800 --> 00:49:32.640
I think snow business is really cute.
我觉得“雪生意”这个说法真的很可爱。

1248
00:49:32.840 --> 00:49:33.220
All right.
好吧。

1249
00:49:33.380 --> 00:49:36.280
But let's go back to the gift exchange.
但让我们回到交换礼物的话题上。

1250
00:49:36.780 --> 00:49:39.780
This is when Kelly gets Angela's poster.
这就是凯莉拿到安吉拉海报的时候。

1251
00:49:40.540 --> 00:49:42.920
But Angela, you do get to take it back.
但是安吉拉，你确实可以把它拿回去。

1252
00:49:43.180 --> 00:49:43.580
Okay.
好吧。

1253
00:49:43.640 --> 00:49:44.420
Here's the thing.
是这样的。

1254
00:49:44.420 --> 00:49:51.600
I wrote in my MySpace blog about this moment, and I wrote that it was one of the hardest
我在我的MySpace博客里写过这一刻，我写道这是我们作为演员最难

1255
00:49:51.600 --> 00:49:58.240
things for us to get through as a cast, that the first time Mindy unrolls the poster
熬过去的事情之一，当敏迪第一次展开那张海报

1256
00:49:58.240 --> 00:50:04.260
and looks at it, and we all see it, we all, every person lost it.
看着它，我们所有人都看到了，我们每个人，每个人都笑场了。

