是啊。

1415
00:56:10.520 --> 00:56:11.520
That was his hope.
那是他的希望。

1416
00:56:11.580 --> 00:56:12.080
That's his goal.
那是他的目标。

1417
00:56:12.220 --> 00:56:13.080
That's his goal.
那是他的目标。

1418
00:56:13.300 --> 00:56:16.720
So, but yeah, Angela is now super ticked because now there's alcohol.
所以，好吧，安吉拉现在超级生气，因为现在有酒了。

1419
00:56:17.160 --> 00:56:19.500
I'm surprised her whole head didn't explode.
我很惊讶她的头没直接炸开。

1420
00:56:19.700 --> 00:56:23.600
Well, it's about to because the next two are what set it into motion.
嗯，快要炸了，因为接下来的两件事才是导火索。

1421
00:56:23.900 --> 00:56:24.140
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1422
00:56:24.140 --> 00:56:29.500
Well, now we have the scene where Jim is trying to get the teapot back from Dwight.
好吧，现在我们到了吉姆试图从德怀特那里拿回茶壶的场景。

1423
00:56:29.700 --> 00:56:32.240
Jim offers to trade him the shamrock keychain.
吉姆提出用三叶草钥匙扣跟他换。

1424
00:56:32.260 --> 00:56:34.200
And he says, come on, it'll be good luck.
他说，拜托，这会带来好运的。

1425
00:56:34.300 --> 00:56:38.540
And that's when Dwight has his line, a real man makes his own luck.
然后德怀特就说了那句台词，真正的男人靠自己创造运气。

1426
00:56:38.740 --> 00:56:47.380
Billy Zane, Titanic, and Angela, you made the entire cast t-shirts with that quote on them.
比利·赞恩，《泰坦尼克号》，还有安吉拉，你给整个剧组做了印有那句台词的T恤。

1427
00:56:47.480 --> 00:56:48.880
And I still have mine.
我到现在还留着我的那件。

1428
00:56:48.960 --> 00:56:50.120
Oh, my gosh, you do?
天哪，你真的留着？

1429
00:56:50.240 --> 00:56:50.640
I do.
我留着。

1430
00:56:50.760 --> 00:56:52.440
It's a gray long-sleeve t-shirt.
那是一件灰色的长袖T恤。

1431
00:56:52.560 --> 00:56:53.820
Yes, with black writing.
是的，上面有黑色的字。

1432
00:56:53.820 --> 00:56:55.460
Just a quote across it.
就只有那句引语。

1433
00:56:55.540 --> 00:56:55.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1434
00:56:55.880 --> 00:57:01.340
So, I had a friend at the time who had a t-shirt press because she had a small business.
当时我有个朋友有一台T恤印刷机，因为她开了家小店。

1435
00:57:01.860 --> 00:57:04.740
And I loved this line so much.
我太喜欢这句台词了。

1436
00:57:04.840 --> 00:57:08.480
I thought it was hilarious of all people for Dwight to quote.
我觉得德怀特引用这句台词简直太搞笑了。

1437
00:57:08.640 --> 00:57:09.900
It would be Billy Zane.
竟然会是比利·赞恩。

1438
00:57:10.140 --> 00:57:12.520
Well, people were asking if we gave each other gifts.
嗯，有人问我们是否互送了礼物。

1439
00:57:12.660 --> 00:57:13.280
That was a gift.
那是一个礼物。

1440
00:57:13.360 --> 00:57:13.920
You gave that out.
你把那个当礼物送出去了。

1441
00:57:13.980 --> 00:57:16.000
I think you actually gave that out at Christmas that year.
我想你那年圣诞节确实送了这个。

1442
00:57:16.100 --> 00:57:16.440
I did.
我送了。

1443
00:57:16.440 --> 00:57:17.840
And you gave everyone an ornament.
而且你还给了每个人一个装饰品。

1444
00:57:18.120 --> 00:57:22.240
Yes, I got that cast photo and I had it printed on an ornament for everyone.
是的，我拿到了那张剧组照，然后把它印在装饰品上送给了大家。

1445
00:57:22.460 --> 00:57:22.720
Yep.
没错。

1446
00:57:23.280 --> 00:57:23.560
Aw.
噢。

1447
00:57:23.820 --> 00:57:33.180
The idea that Dwight wants to keep the teapot in order to wash out his nasal passages with green tea is based on something that Greg Daniels has actually done.
德怀特想留着茶壶用来用绿茶清洗鼻腔的想法，是基于格雷格·丹尼尔斯真正做过的事情。

1448
00:57:33.540 --> 00:57:34.880
Like with a neti pot?
就像用洗鼻壶那样？

1449
00:57:35.300 --> 00:57:38.880
Yeah, I mean, but I've never put green tea in a neti pot.
是啊，我是说，但我从来没在洗鼻壶里放过绿茶。

1450
00:57:39.400 --> 00:57:40.240
I haven't either.
我也没放过。

1451
00:57:40.460 --> 00:57:42.800
I've only used the saline solution that is recommended.
我只用了推荐的那种生理盐水。

1452
00:57:43.140 --> 00:57:46.180
But I could see Greg reading about it and giving it a try.
但我能想象格雷格读到相关内容后去尝试的样子。

1453
00:57:46.180 --> 00:57:56.460
But Rain, the way Rain was in that scene, he shoved that teapot into his nostril.
但雷恩，雷恩在那个镜头里的样子，他把那个茶壶直接塞进了鼻孔里。

1454
00:57:56.700 --> 00:57:56.960
Yeah.
没错。

1455
00:57:56.960 --> 00:58:01.420
And just John's face as Jim is just like, are you kidding me?
还有吉姆那副“你在逗我吗”的表情，简直绝了。

1456
00:58:01.760 --> 00:58:04.280
That, that's who gets my teapot?
那就是拿到我茶壶的人？

1457
00:58:04.520 --> 00:58:05.780
Like, it's so perfect.
真的，太完美了。

1458
00:58:05.800 --> 00:58:07.080
He's so bummed.
他太沮丧了。

1459
00:58:07.080 --> 00:58:19.220
Now, when I watched this with Lee, Lee said he wondered how Dwight didn't find the note in the box or how Dwight didn't open up the teapot.
我和李看这一集的时候，李说他很纳闷德怀特怎么没发现盒子里还有张纸条，或者他怎么没把茶壶打开。

1460
00:58:19.220 --> 00:58:20.600
I thought of all of those things.
这些我也都想过。

1461
00:58:20.780 --> 00:58:24.540
I thought Dwight now has the cassette and the sauce packet.
我当时想，德怀特现在手里有磁带和调料包了。

1462
00:58:25.600 --> 00:58:32.960
I mean, so you have to sort of suspend belief, I guess, at that moment that he took those out and just shoved them aside like, hmm, what's this crap?
我是说，在那一刻你不得不暂时放下逻辑，假设他把那些东西拿出来，随手扔到一边，心里想着“这什么破玩意儿”。

1463
00:58:33.120 --> 00:58:34.740
And just sort of shoved them aside in the box.
然后就随手把它们塞回盒子里了。

1464
00:58:34.740 --> 00:58:38.440
Well, also, I don't think Jim is trying to get the teapot back for Pam.
嗯，而且我觉得吉姆并不是想帮帕姆把茶壶拿回来。

1465
00:58:38.680 --> 00:58:41.400
I think he's just trying to get the teapot back for himself.
我觉得他只是想帮自己拿回茶壶。

1466
00:58:41.460 --> 00:58:42.720
He's just going to keep it now.
他现在打算自己留着了。

1467
00:58:42.980 --> 00:58:50.060
That's what I think the motivation is there because Pam is over, you know, up at the desk with Roy looking through her new iPod.
我觉得这就是他的动机，因为帕姆当时在接待处那边，正和罗伊一起看她的新iPod。

1468
00:58:50.200 --> 00:58:53.840
I think Jim just wants to get it back because I think there's things inside it that are embarrassing.
我觉得吉姆只是想拿回来，因为里面有些东西让他觉得尴尬。

1469
00:58:54.060 --> 00:58:54.720
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

1470
00:58:54.960 --> 00:58:58.280
But he's going to trade the keychain and he's just going to take that teapot home now.
但他会用钥匙扣去交换，然后打算把那个茶壶带回家。

1471
00:58:58.460 --> 00:59:02.200
So Pam is up at reception and she's showing Roy her new iPod.
所以帕姆在接待处，正向罗伊展示她的新iPod。

1472
00:59:02.320 --> 00:59:03.200
He's now at the party.
他现在也到派对现场了。

1473
00:59:03.340 --> 00:59:04.600
He wasn't there for Yankee Swap.
他之前没参加“洋基交换”游戏。

1474
00:59:04.740 --> 00:59:08.740
But he's all excited because now he doesn't have to buy it for Pam for Christmas.
但他很兴奋，因为现在他不用给帕姆买圣诞礼物了。

1475
00:59:09.060 --> 00:59:14.220
He was going to buy her this iPod, he tells her, and now he doesn't have to or he's just going to get her a sweater.
他说他本来打算给她买这个iPod的，现在不用买了，或者他打算随便给她买件毛衣。

1476
00:59:14.700 --> 00:59:15.440
Thanks, Roy.
谢了，罗伊。

1477
00:59:15.680 --> 00:59:19.120
Now the party is like 15 bottles of vodka in.
现在派对已经喝掉大概15瓶伏特加了。

1478
00:59:19.240 --> 00:59:20.740
Todd Packer has showed up.
托德·帕克也出现了。

1479
00:59:20.760 --> 00:59:21.260
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1480
00:59:21.400 --> 00:59:22.480
It's getting crazy.
场面开始失控了。

1481
00:59:23.600 --> 00:59:24.740
Everyone's doing shots.
大家都在喝烈酒。

1482
00:59:24.860 --> 00:59:25.680
Angela's fuming.
安吉拉气坏了。

1483
00:59:25.840 --> 00:59:30.880
I am fuming, but the icing on the cake of my pissed offness is about to happen.
我确实气坏了，但让我火上浇油的事情马上就要发生了。

1484
00:59:31.080 --> 00:59:32.300
Oh, say it.
噢，说出来吧。

1485
00:59:32.300 --> 00:59:36.120
Michael shouts to the whole bullpen.
迈克尔对着整个办公区大喊。

1486
00:59:36.120 --> 00:59:38.420
He says, oh, my gosh.
他说，天哪。

1487
00:59:38.560 --> 00:59:40.860
Yes, Ryan, the king of the party planning.
没错，瑞安，派对策划之王。

1488
00:59:41.460 --> 00:59:42.040
Oh.
噢。

1489
00:59:42.440 --> 00:59:45.500
Thank you to Ryan for this awesome party.
感谢瑞安举办了这场棒极了的派对。

1490
00:59:45.740 --> 00:59:49.260
And the camera pans to me and I am livid.
镜头转向我，我当时气得火冒三丈。

1491
00:59:50.240 --> 00:59:54.480
Ryan, the temp, the king of the party planning committee?
瑞安，那个临时工，派对策划委员会之王？

1492
00:59:54.680 --> 00:59:55.620
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1493
00:59:55.800 --> 00:59:56.040
Yeah.
没错。

1494
00:59:56.040 --> 00:59:57.780
Oh, that's it.
噢，这下完了。

1495
00:59:57.920 --> 00:59:59.520
She is pissed.
她气炸了。

1496
00:59:59.820 --> 01:00:00.680
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1497
01:00:01.200 --> 01:00:03.080
And it's only going to get worse.
而且情况只会变得更糟。

1498
01:00:03.420 --> 01:00:06.640
That's not even still the worst thing that's happened to Angela.
这还不是安吉拉在这集里遇到的最糟糕的事。

1499
01:00:06.880 --> 01:00:07.100
Nope.
没错。

1500
01:00:07.100 --> 01:00:09.460
I had a headache by the end of this episode.
这一集看完我头都疼了。

1501
01:00:09.460 --> 01:00:10.280
You must have.
你肯定得有。

1502
01:00:10.280 --> 01:00:14.640
You were just scowling and pushing anger out of your temples this whole episode.
这一整集你都在皱着眉头，太阳穴都快气炸了。

1503
01:00:15.440 --> 01:00:20.380
Um, you know, when Todd Packer shows up and he has that line, what's up, my nerds?
嗯，你知道，当托德·帕克出现并说了那句台词：“嘿，我的书呆子们，怎么了？”的时候？

1504
01:00:20.420 --> 01:00:20.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1505
01:00:20.720 --> 01:00:21.600
My nerds.
我的书呆子们。

1506
01:00:21.720 --> 01:00:23.700
That was an improv, sort of.
那算是即兴发挥。

1507
01:00:23.960 --> 01:00:27.460
In the script, what was written was, what's up, nerds?
剧本里写的是：“嘿，书呆子们，怎么了？”

1508
01:00:28.760 --> 01:00:33.700
And he just gave it that extra special touch of, what's up, my nerds?
而他只是额外加了点特别的润色，变成了：“嘿，我的书呆子们，怎么了？”

1509
01:00:33.760 --> 01:00:34.080
I know.
我知道。

1510
01:00:34.160 --> 01:00:35.400
Well, that's also Dave Koechner.
嗯，那也是戴夫·科恩纳的风格。

1511
01:00:35.560 --> 01:00:39.440
I mean, I think even the line when he's like, Packer need a drinky.
我是说，我觉得甚至连他说“帕克需要喝一杯”那句台词也是。

1512
01:00:39.440 --> 01:00:39.800
Yeah.
没错。

1513
01:00:40.500 --> 01:00:42.880
The line was probably like, he was getting me a drink.
那句台词原本可能只是说他要给我拿杯喝的。

1514
01:00:43.020 --> 01:00:43.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1515
01:00:43.400 --> 01:00:43.740
You know?
你懂吧？

1516
01:00:44.600 --> 01:00:46.520
He brought so much to that role.
他为那个角色注入了太多东西。

1517
01:00:46.660 --> 01:00:47.200
It was amazing.
太棒了。

1518
01:00:47.320 --> 01:00:50.680
And well, you know when he has to lay down on the desk and get the silly string on him,
还有，你知道当他不得不躺在桌子上，身上被喷满彩带喷雾的时候，

1519
01:00:50.740 --> 01:00:51.600
like when he passes out?
就像他昏过去的时候那样？

1520
01:00:51.740 --> 01:00:52.900
I remember shooting that.
我记得拍那场戏的情景。

1521
01:00:53.020 --> 01:00:54.560
He had to lay there forever.
他得在那儿躺好久。

1522
01:00:54.780 --> 01:00:58.060
So he laid down on those desks, which were not comfortable, right?
他躺在那些桌子上，那可一点都不舒服，对吧？

1523
01:00:58.200 --> 01:00:59.780
And then they silly stringed his head.
然后他们往他头上喷了彩带。

1524
01:01:00.200 --> 01:01:03.400
And then we had all these scenes where that's what he's doing.
之后我们拍的所有场景他都得保持那样。

1525
01:01:03.560 --> 01:01:07.980
Well, if he got up, all the stuff that he was decorated in would have fallen off.
嗯，如果他起身的话，他身上装饰的那些东西就全掉下来了。

1526
01:01:07.980 --> 01:01:09.820
It would have been impossible to recreate.
那样的话就不可能复原了。

1527
01:01:09.820 --> 01:01:13.200
So he had to just lay there, even when we were on a break.
所以即使是在我们休息的时候，他也只能躺在那儿。

1528
01:01:13.380 --> 01:01:14.640
Even when we were on a break.
即使是在我们休息的时候。

1529
01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:16.020
And he was such a trooper.
他真是个硬汉。

1530
01:01:16.160 --> 01:01:16.860
Talk about a trooper.
说起硬汉。

1531
01:01:17.040 --> 01:01:23.200
And I wrote in my MySpace blog that Kate and I, because Kate and I knew Dave from Improv Days.
我在我的MySpace博客里写过，凯特和我，因为凯特和我从即兴表演时期就认识戴夫了。

1532
01:01:23.260 --> 01:01:25.340
We had all like done improv shows together.
我们都曾一起做过即兴表演秀。

1533
01:01:25.560 --> 01:01:29.620
That Kate and I walked over and talked to him while he had to lay on his back.
凯特和我走过去跟他聊天，当时他正不得不躺在背上。

1534
01:01:29.900 --> 01:01:33.060
And we just sort of like caught up and that it was so fun to see him.
我们只是叙了叙旧，能见到他真是太开心了。

1535
01:01:33.060 --> 01:01:40.680
But I want you guys to know, if you're wondering what Todd Packer looks like at 20 minutes, 19 seconds, to really paint a picture here.
但我得让你们知道，如果你想知道20分19秒时的托德·帕克是什么样子，我来给你们描绘一下画面。

1536
01:01:40.760 --> 01:01:40.960
Yeah.
没错。

1537
01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:46.760
He's laying on his back kind of across a desk area partition right in the middle of the room.
他正仰面躺在房间中央的一块办公桌隔断上。

1538
01:01:46.920 --> 01:01:54.640
He has blue silly string on his head, Christmas lights around his torso, Christmas garland around his torso,
他头上喷着蓝色的彩带，躯干上缠着圣诞彩灯，躯干上还缠着圣诞花环，

1539
01:01:55.300 --> 01:02:04.580
Dwight's desk nameplate on his stomach, and there's like a red empty solo cup kind of just like in his, like the crook of his arm.
德怀特的办公桌名牌放在他肚子上，还有一个红色的空塑料杯就在他胳膊弯里。

1540
01:02:04.920 --> 01:02:05.500
You know.
你懂的。

1541
01:02:05.500 --> 01:02:08.800
And he had to lay like that with all those things on top of him.
他不得不带着所有这些东西躺在那儿。

1542
01:02:08.940 --> 01:02:11.580
He passes out so quickly.
他昏过去得太快了。

1543
01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:15.140
You have to imagine he showed up already half drunk.
你得想象一下，他到场时肯定已经半醉了。

1544
01:02:15.340 --> 01:02:16.260
You know he did.
你知道他肯定是。

1545
01:02:16.260 --> 01:02:17.020
You know he did.
你知道他肯定是。

1546
01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:17.900
You know he did.
你知道他肯定是。

1547
01:02:17.900 --> 01:02:26.060
Okay, guys, so now we have the scene where Pam reveals to Jim that she got her teapot back.
好了，各位，现在到了帕姆向吉姆透露她拿回茶壶的那场戏了。

1548
01:02:26.680 --> 01:02:33.580
She trades Dwight the iPod for the teapot, and now she's going to look inside and find all the iteMs.
她用iPod跟德怀特换回了茶壶，现在她要往里面看，找出所有的物品。

1549
01:02:33.600 --> 01:02:36.740
And it's very charming and sweet, and she is so delighted.
那场戏非常迷人且甜蜜，她看起来非常高兴。

1550
01:02:36.980 --> 01:02:42.420
But in this moment, Jim secretly steals the note back and puts it in his pocket.
但在那一刻，吉姆偷偷把纸条拿了回来，放进了自己的口袋里。

1551
01:02:42.640 --> 01:02:43.300
I know.
我知道。

1552
01:02:43.300 --> 01:02:44.800
He lost his courage.
他失去了勇气。

1553
01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:45.740
He did.
他确实失去了。

1554
01:02:45.740 --> 01:02:53.100
Now, when we reached out to fans to ask them what they wanted to know about the Christmas episode,
现在，当我们联系粉丝询问他们想了解关于圣诞特辑的什么内容时，

1555
01:02:53.340 --> 01:03:00.620
I would say that about 80% of the comments and emails we received were along the lines of,
我想说我们收到的评论和邮件中大约80%的内容都是关于，

1556
01:03:00.960 --> 01:03:02.820
what is in the teapot note?
茶壶里的纸条写了什么？

1557
01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:06.600
Because as you know, in this episode, Pam does not read it.
因为如你所知，在那一集中，帕姆并没有读它。

1558
01:03:06.740 --> 01:03:07.640
It is not revealed.
它没有被揭晓。

1559
01:03:07.640 --> 01:03:16.300
But then, in season nine, there's a scene where Jim has the documentary film crew put together footage of their romance,
但后来，在第九季中，有一个场景是吉姆让纪录片摄制组剪辑了他们浪漫史的片段，

1560
01:03:16.300 --> 01:03:22.260
and he shows it to Pam, and Pam sees that there was a note that Jim steals back,
他把它展示给帕姆看，帕姆看到有一张纸条被吉姆偷了回去，

1561
01:03:22.420 --> 01:03:25.800
and then he hands it to her, and she reads it.
然后他把它交给了她，她读了它。

1562
01:03:25.920 --> 01:03:27.120
How brilliant is that?
这有多精彩？

1563
01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:28.200
And you know who that is?
你知道那是谁吗？

1564
01:03:28.240 --> 01:03:29.240
That's Greg Daniels.
那是格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

1565
01:03:29.320 --> 01:03:29.480
Yeah.
是的。

1566
01:03:29.480 --> 01:03:33.900
Because he was such a master at beautiful callback moments.
因为他是这种绝妙呼应时刻的大师。

1567
01:03:34.520 --> 01:03:35.660
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

1568
01:03:35.800 --> 01:03:39.480
Well, from the time that Jim stole the note, it drove people crazy.
嗯，从吉姆偷走纸条的那一刻起，它就让人们抓狂。

1569
01:03:39.780 --> 01:03:43.020
They always wanted to know what had been written in the note.
他们一直想知道纸条上写了什么。

1570
01:03:43.220 --> 01:03:44.700
Would Pam ever get the note?
帕姆会收到那张纸条吗？

1571
01:03:44.860 --> 01:03:47.540
For years and years, will he ever give her the note?
多年来，他会把纸条给她吗？

1572
01:03:47.840 --> 01:03:51.320
Around the time of the wedding, people wanted him to give it to her as a wedding gift.
在婚礼前后，人们希望他能把它作为结婚礼物送给她。

1573
01:03:52.000 --> 01:03:53.600
Greg saved it till the end.
格雷格把它留到了最后。

1574
01:03:53.600 --> 01:03:59.380
And if I'm going to say something that I've never said before, I also feel like I'm maybe going to cry.
如果我要说一些我从未说过的话，我觉得我也快要哭了。

1575
01:03:59.820 --> 01:04:00.340
What?
什么？

1576
01:04:00.600 --> 01:04:01.060
Wait.
等等。

1577
01:04:01.540 --> 01:04:02.060
Wait.
等等。

1578
01:04:02.360 --> 01:04:02.740
What?
什么？

1579
01:04:03.400 --> 01:04:06.300
Are you going to say what was in the note?
你要说纸条上写了什么吗？

1580
01:04:06.820 --> 01:04:08.500
Are you going to say what was in the note?
你要说纸条上写了什么吗？

1581
01:04:09.780 --> 01:04:10.580
Sort of.
算是吧。

1582
01:04:11.040 --> 01:04:13.560
Because I don't know what was on that card.
因为我不知道那张卡片上写了什么。

1583
01:04:13.800 --> 01:04:14.640
None of us do.
我们谁都不知道。

1584
01:04:15.100 --> 01:04:17.600
I'm the only one who knows, and John knows.
只有我知道，还有约翰知道。

1585
01:04:18.060 --> 01:04:19.620
Oh my gosh, lady.
天哪，女士。

1586
01:04:19.620 --> 01:04:38.060
In that episode in Season 9, I believe Greg suggested to John that he write a personal message from himself to me, just saying what our time together on The Office meant to him.
在第九季的那一集中，我相信格雷格建议约翰写一段他自己给我的私人寄语，只是说我们在《办公室》共度的时光对他意味着什么。

1587
01:04:38.160 --> 01:04:38.920
Oh, Jenna.
噢，珍娜。

1588
01:04:40.320 --> 01:04:41.980
Because we were wrapping up filming.
因为我们当时正在结束拍摄。

1589
01:04:42.120 --> 01:04:45.920
We were wrapping up the series, and we were all so emotional at that time, you know?
我们正在结束这部剧，那时我们都非常感伤，你知道吗？

1590
01:04:46.260 --> 01:04:49.520
We were all sort of saying goodbye in different ways.
我们都在以不同的方式告别。

1591
01:04:49.620 --> 01:04:50.020
We were.
我们确实是。

1592
01:04:50.020 --> 01:04:53.320
And so that was his goodbye.
所以那是他的告别。

1593
01:04:54.460 --> 01:05:05.740
Very similar to when we filmed that scene with Steve, where I said goodbye to him at the airport, and Paul Feig told me, just run up and say goodbye to your friend Steve.
这和我们拍摄史蒂夫那个场景时非常相似，我在机场和他告别，保罗·费格告诉我，就跑过去和你朋友史蒂夫告别吧。

1594
01:05:06.520 --> 01:05:13.580
Jeff Blitz said the same thing to me when I was in the car with Oscar, and I say I love Dwight.
当我坐在奥斯卡的车里说我爱德怀特时，杰夫·布里茨也对我说了同样的话。

1595
01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:22.980
He said, Angela, in this moment, express your love for the show and everyone, and if you couldn't have it in your life anymore.
他说，安吉拉，在这一刻，表达你对这部剧和每个人的爱，就好像你生命中再也不能拥有它了一样。

1596
01:05:24.040 --> 01:05:25.460
And I disintegrated.
然后我崩溃了。

1597
01:05:25.720 --> 01:05:25.880
Yeah.
是的。

1598
01:05:26.780 --> 01:05:33.940
So I'm on camera, and I open up this note that John's written me, and I just start crying.
所以我当时在镜头前，打开了约翰写给我的这张纸条，我就开始哭。

1599
01:05:34.240 --> 01:05:35.400
I just start bawling.
我开始嚎啕大哭。

1600
01:05:35.660 --> 01:05:37.760
It probably, the first take was probably not usable.
那可能，第一遍拍摄大概是没法用的。

1601
01:05:40.160 --> 01:05:41.580
It was the sweetest note.
那是一张最贴心的字条。

1602
01:05:41.760 --> 01:05:48.800
And you know, on camera, Pam says, I'll never say what it said, but just know it was perfect.
你知道，在镜头前，帕姆说，我永远不会说出上面写了什么，但只要知道那很完美就行了。

1603
01:05:50.140 --> 01:05:55.500
Well, I'll never say exactly what John wrote, but I will say just know it was perfect.
嗯，我永远不会说出约翰具体写了什么，但我会说，只要知道那很完美就行了。

1604
01:05:55.500 --> 01:05:55.560
Perfect.
完美。

1605
01:05:56.840 --> 01:05:58.920
So that's what was in the teapot note, guys.
所以，伙计们，茶壶里的字条就是这些内容。

1606
01:05:59.080 --> 01:06:01.180
It was a note from John to me.
那是约翰写给我的字条。

1607
01:06:01.340 --> 01:06:04.820
A personal note about what it meant to work with you on the show.
一张关于在剧中与你共事意味着什么的私人字条。

1608
01:06:04.940 --> 01:06:05.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1609
01:06:05.380 --> 01:06:05.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1610
01:06:05.820 --> 01:06:07.680
About our time together on the show, and it was really sweet.
关于我们一起拍戏的时光，真的很贴心。

1611
01:06:07.900 --> 01:06:10.600
Well, that would completely wreck me.
天哪，那绝对会让我崩溃的。

1612
01:06:10.920 --> 01:06:11.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1613
01:06:11.980 --> 01:06:13.400
Oh, I love that.
噢，我喜欢这个。

1614
01:06:13.540 --> 01:06:14.500
I didn't know that.
我之前不知道。

1615
01:06:14.600 --> 01:06:15.180
Are you okay?
你还好吗？

1616
01:06:15.540 --> 01:06:15.980
Yeah.
我没事。

1617
01:06:16.200 --> 01:06:16.660
Well, crap.
好吧，糟糕。

1618
01:06:16.660 --> 01:06:18.100
How do we talk about anything else?
我们还能聊别的吗？

1619
01:06:18.100 --> 01:06:19.280
That was so beautiful.
那太美好了。

1620
01:06:19.840 --> 01:06:20.140
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1621
01:06:20.440 --> 01:06:21.520
That was so beautiful.
那太美好了。

1622
01:06:21.520 --> 01:06:24.400
I love that that was the direction that Greg gave.
我很高兴格雷格给出了那样的指导方向。

1623
01:06:24.400 --> 01:06:29.480
Those moments became very honest for us under that kind of direction.
在那种指导下，那些时刻对我们来说变得非常真实。

1624
01:06:30.340 --> 01:06:32.640
And we all had little moments like that.
我们每个人都有过那样的小瞬间。

1625
01:06:32.740 --> 01:06:33.980
That's a really big one, though.
不过，那确实是一个非常重大的时刻。

1626
01:06:34.180 --> 01:06:36.860
Well, there were those moments on the show that were surprises.
嗯，剧中确实有一些出人意料的时刻。

1627
01:06:37.400 --> 01:06:37.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1628
01:06:37.660 --> 01:06:43.380
Steve didn't know I was going to run up and tell him that basically that same thing.
史蒂夫不知道我会跑过去告诉他基本相同的话。

1629
01:06:43.760 --> 01:06:45.600
Steve, I'm going to miss you.
史蒂夫，我会想念你的。

1630
01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:47.280
You know, all the things that I said to him.
你知道，我对他说的那些话。

1631
01:06:47.560 --> 01:06:49.880
Oscar didn't know the note that Jeff Blitz gave me.
奥斯卡不知道杰夫·布里茨给我的那张字条。

1632
01:06:49.960 --> 01:06:50.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1633
01:06:50.100 --> 01:06:55.700
So when all that emotion came, it was very, like, completely out of nowhere for him.
所以当那种情绪涌现时，对他来说完全是突如其来的。

1634
01:06:55.880 --> 01:06:56.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1635
01:06:56.500 --> 01:06:56.860
Okay.
好吧。

1636
01:06:57.060 --> 01:06:58.840
Well, geez, Louise.
天哪，真是的。

1637
01:06:59.340 --> 01:07:00.000
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1638
01:07:00.020 --> 01:07:00.760
That's okay.
没关系。

1639
01:07:00.880 --> 01:07:02.580
Where are we at in this episode?
我们这一集讲到哪儿了？

1640
01:07:03.060 --> 01:07:08.200
Well, we're at the moment when Kelly approaches Dwight in the kitchen.
嗯，讲到凯莉在厨房接近德怀特的时刻了。

1641
01:07:08.460 --> 01:07:09.580
Kelly, that hussy.
凯莉，那个狐狸精。

1642
01:07:09.740 --> 01:07:12.180
Oh, with her hair half down, half up.
噢，她还梳着半披半扎的发型。

1643
01:07:12.240 --> 01:07:13.000
I know.
我知道。

1644
01:07:13.160 --> 01:07:16.380
She goes up to my man and lays one on him.
她走到我的男人面前，然后吻了他。

1645
01:07:16.380 --> 01:07:16.960
She does.
她确实这么做了。

1646
01:07:16.960 --> 01:07:17.160
Yes.
是的。

1647
01:07:17.380 --> 01:07:21.140
And Angela sees it, and that is it.
安吉拉看到了，然后一切就结束了。

1648
01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:28.000
You know, a lot of people wrote in and commented that you're standing in front of a poster that
你知道，很多人写信评论说你当时正站在一张海报前，

1649
01:07:28.000 --> 01:07:28.820
says commitment.
海报上写着“承诺”。

1650
01:07:29.300 --> 01:07:29.940
Am I really?
真的吗？

1651
01:07:30.160 --> 01:07:30.380
Yes.
是啊。

1652
01:07:30.460 --> 01:07:30.940
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1653
01:07:30.940 --> 01:07:31.860
I didn't even notice.
我都没注意到。

1654
01:07:32.140 --> 01:07:33.160
That is so funny.
太搞笑了。

1655
01:07:33.280 --> 01:07:35.120
I think I was just so focused on the scene.
我想我当时太专注于这场戏了。

1656
01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:35.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1657
01:07:35.420 --> 01:07:36.200
Wow.
哇。

1658
01:07:36.620 --> 01:07:36.920
Yes.
没错。

1659
01:07:37.180 --> 01:07:38.960
Angela loses it.
安吉拉崩溃了。

1660
01:07:39.440 --> 01:07:40.240
Loses it.
崩溃了。

1661
01:07:40.420 --> 01:07:42.420
And this takes us outside.
接下来场景转到了室外。

1662
01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:47.240
She's left the party, and now I have some stuff to tell you guys about this scene.
她离开了派对，现在我有些关于这场戏的幕后信息要告诉大家。

1663
01:07:47.360 --> 01:07:47.410
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

1664
01:07:48.020 --> 01:07:48.500
All right.
好吧。

1665
01:07:48.740 --> 01:07:50.240
20 minutes, 16 seconds.
20分16秒。

1666
01:07:50.540 --> 01:07:52.900
The ultimate Angela pissed-offness has happened.
安吉拉终极愤怒时刻到来了。

1667
01:07:53.400 --> 01:07:55.240
So here's some behind the scenes of this scene.
所以这里有一些关于这场戏的幕后花絮。

1668
01:07:55.740 --> 01:07:59.620
You have a guy up on the roof, and he's got the soap snow.
屋顶上有个人，他拿着肥皂雪。

1669
01:07:59.940 --> 01:08:00.220
Yep.
没错。

1670
01:08:00.320 --> 01:08:00.920
That he's going to-
他打算——

1671
01:08:00.920 --> 01:08:01.880
Falling into your eyes.
掉进你眼睛里。

1672
01:08:01.880 --> 01:08:03.800
He's going to, yeah, stinging.
他打算，没错，会刺痛眼睛。

1673
01:08:04.740 --> 01:08:08.360
And then there's snow on the ground, because they've put real snow on the ground.
然后地上有雪，因为他们铺了真雪。

1674
01:08:08.700 --> 01:08:11.520
We filmed this scene at the end of the day, and everyone had gone.
我们是在一天结束时拍这场戏的，当时大家都走了。

1675
01:08:11.960 --> 01:08:15.900
It was just me and Charles McDougal, Randall Einhorn, and Mike Schur.
现场只有我和查尔斯·麦克杜格尔、兰德尔·艾因霍恩，还有迈克·舒尔。

1676
01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:18.120
So it was just a kind of a skeleton crew at this point.
所以当时只有精简的工作人员在场。

1677
01:08:18.220 --> 01:08:20.080
Those are always some of my most favorite shoots.
那总是我最喜欢的拍摄时刻之一。

1678
01:08:20.380 --> 01:08:21.260
Yeah, me too.
我也是。

1679
01:08:21.380 --> 01:08:23.320
And we did not have a lot of time.
而且我们时间不多。

1680
01:08:23.740 --> 01:08:25.160
We didn't have a lot of time to get this.
我们没有太多时间来完成这一幕。

1681
01:08:25.160 --> 01:08:26.040
Oh, the clock was ticking.
噢，时间紧迫。

1682
01:08:26.320 --> 01:08:30.380
Yeah, exactly, because we didn't want to go into overtime for everyone, and it was the end
没错，正是如此，因为我们不想让大家加班，而且当时已经是

1683
01:08:30.380 --> 01:08:30.860
of the day.
一天结束的时候了。

1684
01:08:30.860 --> 01:08:37.280
And so Charles McDougal said to me, we're probably only going to do like two takes, maybe three.
所以查尔斯·麦克杜格尔跟我说，我们可能只会拍两遍，顶多三遍。

1685
01:08:37.480 --> 01:08:44.940
But they gave me these ornaments, and my instruction was that my character has just lost it.
他们给了我这些装饰品，给我的指示是我的角色已经彻底崩溃了。

1686
01:08:45.040 --> 01:08:46.800
Michael has ruined Christmas.
迈克尔毁了圣诞节。

1687
01:08:47.360 --> 01:08:49.140
Kelly has kissed my man.
凯莉亲了我的男人。

1688
01:08:49.380 --> 01:08:51.940
Ryan is the king of the party planning committee.
瑞安成了派对策划委员会的王。

1689
01:08:52.780 --> 01:08:53.300
Right?
对吧？

1690
01:08:53.540 --> 01:08:53.800
Yes.
没错。

1691
01:08:53.900 --> 01:08:57.840
He said, I want you to take these ornaments and just throw them and shatter them.
他说，我要你拿着这些装饰品，直接扔出去摔碎它们。

1692
01:08:57.840 --> 01:09:00.660
They were written in the script as glass ornaments.
剧本里写的是玻璃装饰品。

1693
01:09:01.360 --> 01:09:03.040
They were not glass ornaments.
它们根本不是玻璃做的。

1694
01:09:03.340 --> 01:09:03.560
What?
什么？

1695
01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:04.640
Watch the scene.
看这场戏。

1696
01:09:04.800 --> 01:09:05.400
I throw them down.
我把它们扔下去。

1697
01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:07.680
They bounce straight up in the air.
它们直接弹到了半空中。

1698
01:09:07.840 --> 01:09:08.620
What were they?
那它们是什么做的？

1699
01:09:08.760 --> 01:09:11.640
They were like some kind of plastic composite whatever.
它们好像是某种塑料复合材料之类的东西。

1700
01:09:12.020 --> 01:09:12.660
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1701
01:09:12.960 --> 01:09:14.820
So when you look, watch it, you guys.
所以你们看的时候，注意看哦。

1702
01:09:14.920 --> 01:09:16.420
You see them bounce in the air.
你们会看到它们在空中弹起来。

1703
01:09:16.760 --> 01:09:19.140
I assumed, well, that makes sense.
我当时想，嗯，这倒也合理。

1704
01:09:19.140 --> 01:09:24.640
We did not have the budget to get special breakaway glass ornaments, and there's no way
我们没有预算去买那种特制的易碎玻璃装饰品，而且他们也不可能

1705
01:09:24.640 --> 01:09:26.160
they would give you real glass.
给你真的玻璃。

1706
01:09:26.400 --> 01:09:26.620
No.
不可能的。

1707
01:09:26.880 --> 01:09:29.900
So these things bounced like a tennis ball.
所以这些东西像网球一样弹了起来。

1708
01:09:30.320 --> 01:09:32.240
And so Charles is like, cut.
然后查尔斯就喊了停。

1709
01:09:32.380 --> 01:09:33.980
And he goes, okay, two things.
他说，好吧，有两件事。

1710
01:09:34.200 --> 01:09:36.780
One, we need you to stand closer to the wall.
第一，我们需要你站得离墙更近一点。

1711
01:09:36.900 --> 01:09:40.300
Like, if you can in the scene, get as close to the wall as possible, because that's where
就是说，如果场景允许的话，尽可能贴近墙壁，因为那是

1712
01:09:40.300 --> 01:09:42.860
the guy is with the soap coming down.
那个撒肥皂水的人所在的位置。

1713
01:09:43.060 --> 01:09:44.760
The soap doesn't ball very far.
肥皂水喷不了多远。

1714
01:09:44.920 --> 01:09:48.980
So we have another take, and he's like, why aren't you breaking the ornaments?
